# Walkthrough - Neumorphic Sliding Auth Redesign

I have completely pivoted the authentication experience to a **Neumorphic (Soft UI)** aesthetic, returning to the highly requested "Sliding Overlay" mechanism. This design focuses on tactile, extruded surfaces and soft depth.

## Key Implementation Details

### 1. Neumorphic Design System
- **Custom Shadows**: Implemented `shadow-nm-flat` and `shadow-nm-inset` utilities in Tailwind. These create the distinctive and soft "extruded" look in dark mode.
- **Base Background**: Adjusted the background to `#0c0d21` to provide the perfect contrast for soft UI shadows.

### 2. Neumorphic Navbar
- A floating, centered navigation bar with soft, tactile buttons.
- **Pressed State**: Buttons appear to physically sink into the navbar on click (`nm-inset` animation).

### 3. Tactile Sliding Auth
- **AuthContainer**: Centered, large-radius card with a horizontal sliding overlay.
- **Depth Elements**: Added ambient background glows that complement the tactile depth of the neumorphic cards.

### 4. Soft UI Auth Forms
- **Inset Inputs**: Redesigned [LoginForm](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/components/auth/AuthCard.tsx#20-92) and [RegisterForm](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/components/auth/AuthCard.tsx#93-168) with inset shadows to make input fields look like they are carved into the surface.
- **Extruded Buttons**: Main action buttons are "raised" from the surface and respond with soft transitions on hover and tap.

